---
title: Spanakopita
servings: 4
tags: [greek, vegetarian]
cuisine: greek
time: 1 hour 5 minutes
source: Spanakopita (Greek Spinach Pie) by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/spanakopita/
---

Heat the oven to 220°C (430°F), or 200°C fan. Line a #baking tray{} with
#baking paper{}.

== Filling ==

Toss the @spinach{300%g}(trimmed leaves, washed, dried, cut in 1-inch pieces)
with @salt{1/2%tsp} and leave ~{10%minutes} to weep.

A handful at a time, wrap the spinach in a #tea towel{} and twist hard to wring
out as much water as you can.

In a bowl, mix the spinach with the @feta{175%g}(crumbled),
@Greek yogurt{1/2%cup}, @scallion{2}(finely sliced), @egg{1},
@fresh mint{2%tbsp}(finely chopped), @fresh dill{1%tbsp}(finely chopped),
@lemon zest{1/2%tsp}, @lemon juice{1/2%tbsp},
@garlic{2%cloves}(finely chopped), @ground nutmeg{1/2%tsp}(freshly grated),
@black pepper{1/4%tsp},
@salt{1/4%tsp} and @cayenne{1/4%tsp}. It should be moist with no pool of water
in the bowl.

== Pie ==

Cut the @phyllo dough{16}(sheets) to 32 x 25 cm (13 x 10 inches), or to 26 cm
(10 1/2 inch) squares. Keep the stack under a damp towel as you work.

Lay 8 sheets on the tray, brushing each with @unsalted butter{120%g}(melted).

Spread the filling over the base, leaving a 1-inch border, and press it flat.
Butter the border.

Lay on 5 more sheets, brushing each with butter and scattering it with the
@kefalotyri{60%g}(or parmesan, finely grated). Add the last 3 sheets with
butter only.

Press the edges together to seal. Crimp them if you like, and trim the
overhang to about 3/4 inch.

Brush the top with butter and sprinkle with @sesame seeds{1/2%tsp}(white) and
@black sesame seeds{1/2%tsp}.

Bake ~{25%minutes}, until deep golden. Serve hot.

> Squeeze the spinach really dry and the pie can be assembled in the morning and baked that night. Don't freeze it raw: the base goes soggy.
